\f2\b \cf2 \cb3 Findings that change the migration
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The custom benefits agent has no retrieval at all.
\f0\b0 \'a0Its code sends the question straight to Claude Sonnet, with no knowledge base attached, so its "Source:" lines aren't grounded. That probably explains the PTO and PPO problems we saw earlier. The kit uses the existing Benefits Knowledge Assistant instead, which also means one less endpoint to pay for.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 One app code change was needed.
\f0\b0 \'a0The app only accepts worker tools it knows by name, so I added the production name\'a0
\f1\fs23\fsmilli11700 \cf4 \cb5 \strokec4 endpoint-perf-policy-citations
\f0\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0to that list in\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "vscode-webview://0vut3krlpv3hr209m36hnjonnrvvu9v67n44uocnnvbqeseti6eg/src/mariner_genai_dbx/supervisor_service.py"}}{\fldrslt \cf6 \ul \ulc6 \strokec6 supervisor_service.py}}.\cb1 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f2\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The performance Knowledge Assistant is skipped by default to save cost.
\f0\b0 \'a0Neither the Supervisor nor the app calls it.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa51\partightenfactor0

